# MP3 fixtures are binary and must never be line-ending translated. Development
# happens on Windows with core.autocrlf=true while CI runs on ubuntu-latest, so a
# file misclassified as text would be corrupted on checkout and fail only in CI.
#
# Git's content heuristic already classifies the structure-only fixtures added for
# #106 as binary, because zeroing the audio payload puts NUL bytes near the start.
# That is incidental, not guaranteed: a future fixture without an early NUL could
# be sniffed as text. Pin it rather than rely on the heuristic.
*.mp3 binary
